<title>MEXICO: Mexico sees sheep meat output up five fold -Ag Min.</title>
<headline>Mexico sees sheep meat output up five fold -Ag Min.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican Agriculture Minister Francisco Labastida Ochoa estimated lamb and mutton output in the next four years would increase five fold.</p>
<p>In a statement obtained Tuesday, the ministry said Labastida told a farmers' meeting that the government's programs to work with sheep farmers would bring the sharp increase of sheep meat output.</p>
<p>Farmers are expected to join programmes aimed at boosting production, especially in the states of Guanajuato, Zacatecas, Hidalgo, Puebla and the State of Mexico.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530. E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com))</p>
